  "readme": [
    {
      "section": "@softspark/dsh-file-preview",
      "text": "[](LICENSE)\n[](https://www.npmjs.com/package/@softspark/dsh-file-preview)\n\nRead-only file preview inside a DeepSeek Harness conversation. Click a file the agent produced or mentioned and it opens in the browser, instead of launching a desktop application.\n\nWorks on the **published harness**. No patch, no fork, no modified checkout."
    },
    {
      "section": "What's New in v2.0.0",
      "text": "- DSH `0.1.2-rc.1` support through its Session Remote opener and immutable host event snapshots.\n- Enforced 70% coverage, filesystem authorization integration tests, and browser registration tests.\n- Complete post-release SOP and published browser TypeScript declarations.\n\nVersion 2 requires DSH `0.1.2-rc.1`. Keep plugin `1.0.0` when using DSH `0.1.1-rc.2`."
    },
    {
      "section": "Contents",
      "text": "- [Why](#why)\n- [Requirements](#requirements)\n- [Install](#install)\n- [What it previews](#what-it-previews)\n- [How it claims a click](#how-it-claims-a-click)\n- [Security](#security)\n- [Documentation](#documentation)\n- [Contributing](#contributing)"
    },
    {
      "section": "Why",
      "text": "Without it, opening a file from a conversation hands the path to the host operating system. That is the wrong gesture when the harness runs on a remote machine, in a container, or when the file is a diff you want to glance at without leaving the page."
    },
    {
      "section": "Requirements",
      "text": "- Node.js 22.19.0 or newer\n- DeepSeek Harness `0.1.2-rc.1`\n- `pnpm` for the profile plugin manager"
    },
    {
      "section": "Install",
      "text": "```bash\ndsh plugin --profile web add @softspark/dsh-file-preview --save-exact\n```\n\nRestart DSH. The package registers both of its rows itself."
    },
    {
      "section": "What it previews",
      "text": "| Kind | Formats | Bound |\n|---|---|---|\n| Text and code | `.txt` `.md` `.json` `.yaml` `.toml` `.csv` `.ts` `.js` `.py` `.go` `.rs` `.sql` and more | 1 MiB |\n| Markup | `.html` `.svg`, sanitised to an allowlist | 1 MiB |\n| Images | `.png` `.jpg` `.gif` `.webp` | 8 MiB |\n| Documents | `.pdf` | 8 MiB |\n\nAnything else reaches the harness's own opener untouched, exactly as before the plugin was installed."
    },
    {
      "section": "How it claims a click",
      "text": "Every conversation file-open in DSH 0.1.2 reaches `remote.session.openWorkspacePath({ path })`. The browser half wraps its getter while preserving the native request, cancellation signal, and caller context. Removing the package restores the original descriptor.\n\nIf a future harness stops exposing that method, the plugin refuses to mount rather than silently swallowing clicks."
    },
    {
      "section": "Security",
      "text": "A preview must not become an arbitrary host-file read. Authorization is computed on the host from session facts alone: a file is readable when it sits inside the addressed session's workspace, or when that same session produced it through a successful write or edit. Failures never carry file bytes, and both refusal grounds return the same code so a rejection cannot be used to probe for a file's existence."
    },
    {
      "section": "Security",
      "text": "Full model in [`kb/reference/security.md`](kb/reference/security.md) and [`SECURITY.md`](SECURITY.md)."
    },
    {
      "section": "Documentation",
      "text": "| Document | Purpose |\n|---|---|\n| [Architecture](kb/reference/architecture.md) | The two halves and the interception seam |\n| [Security model](kb/reference/security.md) | Authorization, bounds, sanitization |\n| [Setup](kb/howto/setup.md) | Install and confirm |\n| [Common issues](kb/troubleshooting/common-issues.md) | Why a preview refuses or does not open |\n| [Release SOP](kb/procedures/sop-release.md) | How a version ships |\n| [Post-release SOP](kb/procedures/sop-post-release-testing.md) | Registry provenance, browser behavior, and authorization checks |"
    },
    {
      "section": "Contributing",
      "text": "See [CONTRIBUTING](.github/CONTRIBUTING.md). `pnpm run verify` is the gate."
    },
    {
      "section": "License",
      "text": "Apache-2.0. See [LICENSE](LICENSE) and [NOTICE](NOTICE)."
    }
